# Vendored third-party trees. Checked in deliberately (see the commits that
# added them), but they are not PRSH source and should not be read as such.
#
#   linguist-vendored — keeps them out of GitHub's language stats and collapses
#                       them by default in PR review.
#   -diff             — `git diff` reports "Binary files differ" instead of
#                       printing the body. Override per-command with --text.
#
# Between them these three trees are ~185k lines, about two thirds of the
# 2.0.0 branch diff, and none of it is hand-written here.

# impeccable — the design-quality skill + post-edit hook. Two near-identical
# copies on purpose: the tool's installer hardcodes a skill path next to each
# agent's own config, so Claude Code and GitHub Copilot each get their own.
# ~65k lines apiece.
.claude/skills/impeccable/** linguist-vendored -diff
.github/skills/impeccable/** linguist-vendored -diff

# three.js — vendored rather than bundled because layouts under public/layout/
# are static files served straight to OBS with no build step. ~56k lines.
public/layout/lib/three/** linguist-vendored -diff

# Line endings: the repository stores LF, whoever's machine wrote the file.
# Ten files came over from TournamentStreamHelper as CRLF, and any tool that
# round-tripped one in text mode flipped it wholesale — a 6-line PRSH.spec
# change showed as 808. Git now normalizes on commit, so that can't recur.
# Nothing here needs CRLF: PowerShell and Inno Setup both read LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
